WEBVTT

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.620
Sei, if you could have anything,
what would you want?

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.830
Where's this coming from?

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:22.080
We received bonus funding for our
assistance with the Salamander incident.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:26.920
That, and the Knights will be making
regular purchases of your potions.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:31.050
As such, we've got a bit
of a budget surplus.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.800
Oh. Well, that's nice, I suppose.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.480
You have just as much a right
to the surplus as we do, Sei.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:43.270
You're responsible for our
recent success, after all.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.230
Is there anything you want to have?

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.070
There is <i>one </i>thing...

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:31.210
A pleasant surprise, I hope?

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:34.300
Absolutely! I can't believe you
put this together in a week's time.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:37.470
Doing all this in a week would
make any Japanese contractor cry.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.560
Guess Salutania's work standards
can be pretty brutal, too...

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:44.600
I'm surprised you wanted
a kitchen, of all things.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.230
I'm no noblewoman, Ser Director.
I cook for myself.

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:49.730
I suppose that's true.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:52.530
By our kingdom's standards,
you're quite well-educated,

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.530
even concerning matters outside
of your specialism in herbalism.

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:56.660
I sometimes forget you
are of common stock.

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:59.830
And I only have a hobbyist's
knowledge of herbs...

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:04.410
We'll hire a chef to work in your kitchen.
There's no need for you to cook.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:07.210
Oh, uh...

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.750
I actually really enjoy cooking!

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:15.090
I'm not about to tell him I'm doing it
because the food here is <i>awful</i>.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:18.140
You'll be cooking, then? I'd like
to give it a try, if you don't mind.

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:18.930
Huh?

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:20.800
Right then, what are you making first?

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.520
W-Well, I'm going to need
some ingredients first.

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:26.890
I see. Then I wait with bated breath.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:31.150
Didn't I see you eating lunch
just earlier, Ser Director?

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:37.360
W-Well, as a researcher, I'm very
interested in your homeland's cuisine!

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.450
What does that have
to do with <i>herbal </i>research?

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.870
You can use our budget
for your ingredients!

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:47.710
All right. But please don't
get your hopes up too high!

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:48.830
Yes!

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:57.720
Well, if he's going to get that excited,
I might as well make him something!

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.430
What are you making?

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.180
Herb-crusted chicken with a light salad.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.020
Herb-crusted?

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:12.650
Yes, I'm using some of our
medicinal herbs in the cooking.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:14.020
Is that all right?

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.690
Yes, of course.

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:20.110
I've just never heard of a chef using
medicinal herbs in their dishes.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:23.240
Is that right?

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:29.870
This world resembles
my own in so many ways...

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:33.920
...that it's all the more
apparent when it doesn't.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.260
Here you are.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:50.640
Delicious! Absolutely amazing!

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.350
I'm glad you like it!

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:55.110
To think using medicinal herbs would
enhance the flavor to this degree...

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:58.320
No, it's not just that...

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:05.030
In my home world, we used lots of
medicinal herbs in our everyday cooking.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:08.700
There's also a form of medicinal cooking
that uses herbs to ward off disease.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:12.960
I've got an idea! Why don't you teach
our chefs some of those recipes?

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:15.880
If all of them are as delicious as this,
I'm sure everyone would want some!

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:23.840
Marjoram here can be used in soups
and sauces, as well as in salad dressing.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.890
Sei, you around?

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:27.310
Yes, what is it?

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:34.940
The Director wants you to deliver these
missives to the Third Order barracks.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:38.070
I'm a little busy right now.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.900
He insisted that it had to be you, though.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.070
He did?

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:45.780
Well, all right. I'll go, then.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:51.160
Find the Knight Commander
up in his office.

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:55.420
Got it. Don't eat too much, now!

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:57.460
I won't! Thanks, Sei!

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:05.550
Oh, there she is. Come on in.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:06.720
Pardon the intrusion.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.310
Here are the documents you requested.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.310
There we go. Thank you, Sei.

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:17.110
Of course. I'll take my leave, then.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.190
Hold on.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:27.280
<i>This </i>is Sei.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:30.620
I see. That was <i>you</i>.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:35.290
My name is Albert Hawke. I'm the Knight
Commander of the Third Order of Knights.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:40.210
Such beautiful blue-grey eyes...

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:44.300
I've seen lots of handsome men
in this world by now,

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.840
but out of all of them,
he's the one who's most my type.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:48.510
What a wonderful world.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:53.600
Oh, i-it's a pleasure to meet you.
My name is Sei.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:02.530
I'm sure you recall the Third Order's
most recent expedition, yes?

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:04.700
The incident with the Salamander?

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:08.620
You treated a gravely wounded
man with a high-grade potion.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:12.160
Oh!

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.250
This is that man.

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:20.710
Wow. You wouldn't know
he was ever on death's door.

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:23.920
He healed up beautifully. He looks <i>great</i>.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:27.260
Thank you for saving my life.
I would be dead if not for you.

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:28.510
Oh, don't mention it.

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:31.100
Shoot, I was staring too long.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:35.890
Ser Director?

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:37.730
Oh, no, pardon me.

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:41.110
My apologies.

00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:44.530
Sei, you wanted more ingredients
for your high-grade potions, correct?

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:45.820
Th-That's right.

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:48.280
Then you may journey into the
Southern Woods to gather them.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:49.990
Huh? B-But Ser--

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:52.450
I know, I know,
there are beasts there, yes.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:56.000
But that is where he comes into play.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.000
Huh?

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.920
This is his way of thanking you.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:01.250
If you would do me that honor.

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:05.010
Sure, but you've <i>already </i>thanked me.

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:08.180
He'd like to thank you
<i>personally </i>for your service.

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:10.260
Johan! That was unnecessary!

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:12.430
Personally?

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:11.720
Now, now.

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:17.940
Our Order was already due
for a hunt in the southern woods.

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:21.150
It only makes sense for you
to accompany us then.

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:23.190
That does make sense.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:25.820
I wouldn't have to worry about monsters.

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:27.990
And I <i>did </i>want more of those herbs...

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:36.330
As long as it isn't a bother,
I'd love to join you.

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:37.790
Let us go then, Sei.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.590
Sei! Stick with us, all right?

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:48.970
Got it!

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:51.140
It may be more peaceful here
than in the Western Woods,

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:53.260
but that doesn't mean you're not
going to see <i>any </i>monsters.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:57.850
I know, sorry. I'd just never
seen an herb like that before.

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:00.730
Not to worry.
We're keeping a close watch on you.

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:02.980
As long as you stay close, you'll be safe.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:04.110
Commander Hawke...

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:10.280
Still, I'm surprised we haven't
encountered any monsters,

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:12.160
especially being so deep into the woods.

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:13.490
I'm surprised, too.

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:17.240
I would expect to have
encountered several by now.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:19.870
It's rather strange that we have
yet to see a single one.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.960
Oh, really?

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:24.500
Let us worry about any potential beasts.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:27.500
You and your colleagues focus
on gathering the herbs you need.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.760
Thank you so much.

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:35.010
Th-This is delicious!

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:42.520
Your soup is quite the hit.

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:43.900
Commander Hawke!

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:47.440
Please, Commander, have some.
It's got medicinal herbs in it.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.360
Very well, if you insist.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:57.450
Incredible!

00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:00.950
I'd heard rumors about the
quality of meals at the Institute,

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:03.290
but I never fathomed it was <i>you</i>.

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:07.670
Oh, no, I just shared some recipes
with the Institute's chefs, that's all.

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:13.130
I'll admit, I'm jealous that you get to
eat such luxurious meals every day.

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:15.140
I'm flattered.

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:18.350
So, uh, why is he sitting
right next to me?

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:24.440
You mentioned there were
medicinal herbs in this soup, yes?

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:26.230
Y-Yes, that's correct.

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:29.860
Today I added some shaved
galangal to the soup.

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:34.150
It has a bit of a spicy aftertaste
and pairs well with onions.

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:37.490
It also helps to warm
the body and relieve fatigue...

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:43.660
I see. You truly are quite
knowledgeable about your craft.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.580
O-Oh, I wouldn't say that.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:48.090
Thank you, Sei.

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:57.470
Right, then. Let us head a bit
deeper into the woods!

00:10:57.470 --> 00:10:58.720
Prepare to head out!

00:10:58.720 --> 00:10:59.850
Yes, Commander!

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:07.270
I'm back!

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.520
Not like there's anyone else here...

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:13.860
I'm exhausted.

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:25.330
But in a good way. Not like I was before.

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:01.450
Okay!

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:07.250
Good morn--

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:10.170
Sei.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:16.460
Companionship

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:22.510
We've received a startling report
from the Third Order of Knights.

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:23.680
Yes?

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:25.720
Apparently, during yesterday's expedition,

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:29.690
the knights' physical abilities
were significantly heightened.

00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:30.690
Uh-huh.

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:33.940
As we were investigating
the possible cause,

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:40.820
someone raised the possibility that it
could have been their lunch that day.

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:42.320
Okay.

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:46.450
The researchers came together
to eat this cooking for every meal,

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:48.750
and found that depending on the recipe,

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:52.000
all saw improvements
to various physical abilities.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.000
And that's not all.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:56.920
So... what else?

00:12:56.920 --> 00:13:01.050
The 50% increase in efficacy
measured in your potions

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:05.060
also appears to affect
the recipes you cook.

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:06.640
Yeah, figured...

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:12.100
Let's put discussion of your mysterious
50% efficacy increase on hold for now.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:16.610
Sei, please try not to cook out
in public for the time being.

00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:19.780
If word gets out about your abilities,
it could mean chaos.

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:20.780
Yes, ser.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:28.910
Doesn't look like we'll get
much work done today.

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:30.960
You should take the day off, Sei.

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:32.960
What? But...

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:47.680
Shocking nobody, I'm bored out of my mind.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:54.850
"Principles of Pharmacology
On Herbal Medicine"

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:03.780
Let's learn a bit more about herbs,

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:05.320
and pharmacology, too...

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:13.920
Wow. She looks like a porcelain doll.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:23.760
That's quite the difficult tome you
have there. Are you with the Institute?

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:25.720
Huh? Oh, yes, I am.

00:14:25.720 --> 00:14:30.390
I knew it! Few people can read
Classical Salutanian, after all.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:34.230
Oh, uh, well...

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:39.230
My apologies, I've been remiss.
My name is Elizabeth Ashley.

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:41.860
Pleased to meet you. I'm Sei.

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:44.360
I hope we'll meet again soon!

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:46.570
Of course, likewise.

00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:01.550
Sei!

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:03.880
Commander Hawke!

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:07.800
Good afternoon. What a coincidence,
seeing you here at the Palace.

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:09.300
Are you headed back to the Institute?

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:10.090
Yes, I am.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:11.560
Climb on. I'll give you a ride there.

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:16.520
Huh? Oh, uh, thank you for the offer,
but I've never ridden a horse before!

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:17.690
Take my hand.

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:28.200
Right then, let us be off!

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:32.540
Don't worry. I've got you.

00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:44.340
What business did you have at the Palace?

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:49.220
Uh, I have the day off today,
so I wanted to visit the library.

00:15:49.220 --> 00:15:54.770
Is that so?
What kinds of books did you find?

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:54.770
The Commander's voice
is so close to my ear...

00:15:54.770 --> 00:15:58.150
I'm a little nervous being
so close to him,

00:15:58.150 --> 00:16:02.480
but for some reason, speaking with
him makes me feel so at ease.

00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:05.110
What other hobbies do you enjoy?

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:07.200
Let me think...

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:08.700
Actually, I can't think of any!

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:11.990
Is that right?
Then perhaps on your next day off...

00:16:13.080 --> 00:16:14.950
Pardon me, disregard that.

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:26.170
I said he didn't have to take me
all the way back, but he did anyway.

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:32.390
After that, the Commander would give me
a ride back from the Palace quite often.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:36.980
Stare...

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:41.560
I also ran into Elizabeth at the library
often enough to befriend her.

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:45.360
We're close enough now that
I call her by her nickname.

00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:46.990
Staaaaare...

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:47.900
Yes, Liz?

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:50.570
You have such lovely skin, Sei.

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:51.450
I do?

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:54.080
Yes! It's so very easy
to tan in this hot season,

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:57.250
but your skin hasn't taken on any color
at all! It's only grown more lovely!

00:16:57.250 --> 00:17:00.330
Your skin looks far lovelier
than mine to me, Liz.

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:03.090
Well, I do try to take care of it.

00:17:03.090 --> 00:17:07.710
Maybe it's the cosmetics we use.
I've been making my own.

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:09.970
Wow! That's incredible!

00:17:09.970 --> 00:17:13.510
I use medicinal herbs to craft them.
I can make you some, if you'd like.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.510
I'd love some! Thank you!

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:17.770
You're such a girly-girl, Liz.

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:20.060
Oh? Did you think otherwise before?

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:21.850
Oh, no, I'm sorry!

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:30.240
What is it?

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:34.700
Oh, nothing. I was just thinking upon
the endless struggle for beauty.

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:37.200
But you <i>are </i>beautiful, Liz.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.540
Thank you, Sei.

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:42.580
But I was thinking of
someone other than myself.

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:47.710
I feel terrible gossiping about this,
but I suppose you should know.

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:55.390
The trouble started when a girl
joined the class mid-semester.

00:17:55.390 --> 00:17:58.640
She grew unusually close with a number
of boys who are already betrothed,

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:01.520
causing quite the ruckus at the academy.

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:06.320
Many warned her what would
happen if she continued, to no avail.

00:18:06.320 --> 00:18:10.820
Then, one of the boys' fiancées
stopped attending classes.

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:13.950
She was just the right age for
acne to be a constant problem,

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:18.040
not to mention a constant
source of anxiety for her.

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:22.210
Try as she might, nothing seemed to
prevent her breakouts, but then...

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:28.090
Wow. So she started comparing
herself to that popular new girl...

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:35.090
If her skin condition were resolved,
I think her confidence would return.

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:36.640
That makes sense.

00:18:36.640 --> 00:18:39.850
I might be able to help her
with her skin, actually.

00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:41.100
Really?!

00:18:54.990 --> 00:18:57.870
Hey! You're making cosmetics again?

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:01.450
Yes. I'm trying to make
something to help with acne.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:06.670
Wow. I bet yours will be way more
effective than anything else out there.

00:19:06.670 --> 00:19:08.000
Y-Yeah, probably.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:11.460
I just wanted to get rid of my bags,
but now my eyesight is better, too.

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:13.720
Honestly, I kind of scare myself.

00:19:13.720 --> 00:19:17.260
I'm sure your potions helped,
but it's more than that.

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:15.760
Huh?

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:19.260
You've gotten so much prettier
since first arriving here!

00:19:21.770 --> 00:19:23.680
Wh-Where did <i>that </i>come from?!

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:29.690
Sheesh, don't tease me!

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:42.790
Sei!

00:19:43.580 --> 00:19:48.830
This is Lady Nicole Adler. She's the
woman we discussed the other day.

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:50.880
Please, just Nicole is fine.

00:19:50.880 --> 00:19:53.510
My name is Sei.
I work over at the Institute.

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:03.220
Here's a lotion I crafted.
Please, give it a try.

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:08.770
I'm sure Sei's lotion will be
of great help to you, Nicole.

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:12.320
If you believe so, Lady Elizabeth,
then I am hopeful.

00:20:12.320 --> 00:20:15.280
But if it still doesn't work, then...

00:20:18.910 --> 00:20:21.620
It's only natural to be
afraid of the unknown.

00:20:21.620 --> 00:20:24.240
There's no rush.
Give it a try at your leisure.

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:27.660
Hey!

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:30.130
Liz! Do a patch test first!

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:32.540
My word... this is incredible!

00:20:38.430 --> 00:20:41.970
Your skin looks so lovely, Lady Elizabeth!

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:55.360
You see, Nicole, you shouldn't try
to look a certain way for someone else.

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:58.280
I want to make myself happy.

00:20:58.280 --> 00:21:02.240
I want to look lovely for my own sake.

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:04.490
Isn't that what matters most?

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:06.250
You agree, right, Sei?

00:21:06.250 --> 00:21:09.460
Huh? Oh, absolutely. I totally agree.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:15.380
Lady Sei... Thank you so much!

00:22:51.010 --> 00:22:53.850
Thank you again for your help.
I'd love to invite you over to speak more
over dinner.

00:22:51.010 --> 00:22:53.850
Nicole Adler

00:22:52.980 --> 00:22:54.900
Really? I'm so glad to hear that.

00:22:54.900 --> 00:22:57.060
As am I!

00:22:57.060 --> 00:23:01.900
Word of your cosmetics has spread
throughout the academy and nearby town.

00:23:01.900 --> 00:23:04.860
I'm not sure I'm so glad to hear <i>that</i>.

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:07.740
But it if helps everyone feel prettier,
then sure, that's good.

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:12.000
They would still pale in
comparison to you, Sei.

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:15.620
After all, your beauty is due to more
than just well-crafted cosmetics.

00:23:18.090 --> 00:23:21.460
You're in the midst of a
budding romance, are you not?

00:23:21.460 --> 00:23:22.670
Excuse me?

00:23:22.670 --> 00:23:28.300
Rumors tell of a lovely young lady
melting the Ice Knight's frozen heart!

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:30.010
Who's the Ice Knight?

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:31.350
Don't be coy, now.

00:23:31.350 --> 00:23:34.980
Why, many have spotted you riding
tandem with him on horseback!

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:39.360
W-Wait, what?!

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.990
Next Time

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.990
Capital
